      "evidence_sha256": "5c8593fdc3e1979e088f3a1945a79b9429172485ebecc22e7d54fc2951799020",
      "assessment": "R2 G4 directly compares to R0 and distinguishes restoring interval1 (recovery +0.018919) from improving beyond R0 (latest remains -0.001428). It properly treats public early-window benefit as external branch evidence, not an observation in its private history. Incumbent selection and unavailable candidate traces are clearly labelled.",
      "decision_update": "[6,5,6,5] duplicates G2:H2 and is represented through that proposal in R3; [5,6,6,5] is not selected. This is evidence-led component continuation, but one cannot claim the unselected continuation would have improved Mean. Preserve its distinction between recovery and net gain.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The text says no breadth gate is imposed, yet its H1 falsifier rejects a Mean gain carried only by one candidate. This contradiction should be removed: concentration is a risk/diagnostic attribute, not an automatic failure of the primary Mean objective.",
