    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r02/synthesis",
      "evidence_sha256": "fcd36f47b84e9fd4ed9d20a2d6a25839f9140f68d87a0a444cb389ba51c06b73",
      "assessment": "R2 council detects the duplicated [6,5,6,5], rejects the already tested tick7 array, and explicitly pays for one lower-expectation conditional probe to discriminate interaction. It corrects the early monotonicity narrative using the measured loss. Some bookkeeping remains wrong: G4 inherited the mid combined branch, not the r01 early branch; [6,6,5,5], not [6,5,5,5], has the slightly highest measured Mean.",
      "decision_update": "R3 runs [6,5,5,5], [6,5,6,5], [6,6,5,6], [7,5,6,5]. The selection supplies a same-wave contrast across early levels and mid addition, plus a justified parent-replay reference. This is a counterexample to Top1’s blanket avoidance of combinations; evaluate its outcomes before revising exploration rules.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Its public memory calls indices1–3 inert and an interior optimum established more strongly than the limited conditional evidence warrants. Historical and same-wave contrasts have different parent contexts. The supplied ledger does not support treating incumbent deficit as evidence against a fixed schedule.",
