    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r03/G1",
      "evidence_sha256": "43cfaa8331d193c747a7197f41233489d5631abd8081b1d485d194599b3dc830",
      "assessment": "R3 G1 obtains the actual reciprocal pair: returning early tick7 to6 recovers 0.063475 and reproduces its earlier fixed Mean. Concentration is computed correctly and the incumbent remains a benchmark. But it repeatedly interprets a single strong contributor as a falsifier, wrongly calls interval1 switching the largest, and converts a locally tested reversal into an interior optimum.",
      "decision_update": "Proposes [5,5,5,5] and [6,4,5,5]; neither is chosen for R4. A base-array replay needs evidence that its effective prefix/RNG context supplies new information, while the down probe is a valid different conditional direction. Do not count the unselected base test as performed.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The observed repeated array at equal score is not an independent replicate. Same early restoration can erase parent differences in the recomputed suffix; changed per-chain TOP1 labels alone do not guarantee changed effective starting states.",
