    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r03/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "81632f013960a4ba17c338b01e43dd0e19d01dd3d7220dd559f86654a5700bc3",
      "assessment": "R3 G2 accurately computes the two largest R0 contributions as about 0.0354 and 0.0323, improving on its earlier arithmetic. Its last-action ledger is nevertheless wrong: r02 [6,6,5,5] to r03 [6,5,6,5] changes two intervals, not just index2. The -0.000099 belongs to that exchange; direct r01-to-r03 is about -0.000022. This misattribution reaches public memory.",
      "decision_update": "Both proposals [6,4,6,5] and [6,5,6,4] execute as R4 G2 and G3. They supply previously untested conditional downward responses without changing the supported early level. Their direction is reasonable despite the flawed last-action rationale; the future result cannot validate that rationale retroactively.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The analyst asserts geometry cannot rank arms from small displacement, without comparing geometry, and introduces a 0.055-plus-median threshold for a meaningful late response. A modest valid Mean change still matters; saturation, low dose and proxy mismatch are distinct possibilities.",
